cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata from this file."
title: "Go-Ecology: a Go-inspired territorial competition model on graphs"
abstract: >-
  Simulation and analysis code for a Go-inspired territorial competition model on
  graphs, studying how network topology (Erdos-Renyi, SBM, DC-SBM, lattice, torus)
  and scheduling (synchronous vs energy-weighted asynchronous) shape competition
  outcomes — coexistence, dominance, and bimodality — in two- and three-player
  rock-paper-scissors and all-vs-all contests. Backs the paper "Inspired by Go:
  playing ecology with complex topologies – two- and three-species territorial
  competition on regular and irregular graphs."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Aho"
    given-names: "Matti"
    affiliation: "Aalto University"
license: GPL-3.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/MattiAAho/go-ecology-resource"
